<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka Grain H1 net turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka Grain H1 net turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited results for six months to June 30, 1996, of Ceylon Grain Elevators Ltd.</p>
<p>		(in millions of rupees unless stated):</p>
<p>				    H1 1996		  H1 1995</p>
<p>    Turnover		   1,308.20   vs	  1,239.59</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss	loss 15.44   vs    profit 89.94</p>
<p>    Tax				7.82   vs	     20.77</p>
<p>NOTE - Ceylon Grain Elevators Ltd, a feedmiller and poultry breeder, is a unit of Singapore's Prima Ltd. It consolidates accounts with Three Acre Farms Ltd. Power cuts from late March until the end of period and rumours of poultry disease were largely responsible for the loss, a company statement said.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom tel 941-434319</p>
